# Local-first coding report

## Desktop SoT

Ordinary MUTATE work binds to **DIRECT_CANONICAL**:
`C:\Users\compg\Desktop\top-code workspace\<repo>`.

Session-scratch is evidence / logs / optional isolation only.
Do not treat a scratch worktree as the product tree unless the task
explicitly used `--workspace-mode ISOLATED_WORKTREE` (then promote on accept).

## Report order (mandatory for coding tasks)

Start every substantial coding reply with:

```markdown
## Zmienione pliki
- <repo-relative path> — <1-line why>
```

Only list files actually written or deleted on the desktop checkout in this turn/task.
Then: root cause / what changed / proof / status.
Commit SHA and GitHub are secondary — after the file list and proof.

## Commit vs publication

- Local scoped commit = secondary history of finished owned work (via `task-commit-plan` → act on `decision`).
- GitHub push/PR only on explicit `PUBLISH` / `SHIP`.
- Do not ask "czy commit?" when `decision` is `COMMIT_NOW`.

## Continue / resume hygiene

On `kontynuuj` / `dokończ`: restate the **current user goal in this thread** in one line before acting.
Do **not** silently resume archived task IDs, `MEMORY.md` NEXT, or unrelated P4/P5 proof threads.
